 *//* Current Fix. As mutual inclusion of files prevent to define following. Need fix *//* CAPABILITY: 11n HT available *//*
 * 802.11 protocol implementation definitions.
 *//* default state *//* scanning *//* try to authenticate *//* try to assoc *//* associated *//*
 * Return the size of the 802.11 header for a management or data frame.
 *//* NB: we don't handle control frames *//* Frame has HT control field in the header *//*
 * Like ieee80211_hdrsize, but handles any type of frame.
 *//*
 * Template for an in-kernel authenticator.  Authenticators
 * register with the protocol code and are typically loaded
 * as separate modules as needed.
 *//* printable name *//*
 * Template for an in-kernel authenticator backend.  Backends
 * register with the protocol code and are typically loaded
 * as separate modules as needed.
 *//* printable name *//*
 * Template for an MAC ACL policy module.  Such modules
 * register with the protocol code and are passed the sender's
 * address of each received frame for validation.
 *//* printable name *//* flags for ieee80211_fix_rate() *//* sort rate list *//* use fixed rate *//* calc negotiated rate *//* delete ignore rate *//* intersection of rates *//* check for basic rates *//* XXX: is there any reason to have multiple instances of cap_info_count??? *//* ver. of the current param set *//*WME params for each access class *//* STATUS: WME aggressive mode *//* VI/VO frames in beacon interval *//* aggressive mode switch threshold *//* aggressive mode switch hysteresis *//* configured WME parameters applied to itself*//* configured WME parameters broadcasted to STAs*//* channel parameters applied to itself*//* channel parameters broadcasted to STAs*//* don't use aggressive params and use WME params *//* VSP WME throt bitmap *//* update hardware tx params after wme state change *//* used for send formatted string custom event IWEVCUSTOM *//*
 * Beacon frames constructed by ieee80211_beacon_alloc
 * have the following structure filled in so drivers
 * can update the frame later w/ minimal overhead.
 *//* capabilities *//* start of atim/dtim *//* start of WME parameters *//* start of fixed-size tim trailer *//* atim/dtim length in bytes *//* trailer length in bytes *//* start of bss load *//* where channel switch IE will go *//* where ath caps is *//* start of xr element *//* start of clear channel assessment element. *//* start of HT Capability element *//* start of HT Info element *//* start of TPC Report IE*//* start of ERP element *//* start of APP IE buf *//* APP IE buf length in bytes *//* host-onlyrecoveredRRMIE pointer *//* XXX exposed due to of beacon code botch *//* MU MIMO *//*
 * Notification methods called from the 802.11 state machine.
 * Note that while these are defined here, their implementation
 * is OS-specific.
