 *//* length in bytes *//* ssid contents *//* policy hookup, see below *//* scanner private state *//* scs private state independent of the scan state *//* scan only, no selection *//* active scan (probe req) *//* ``hey sailor'' mode *//* bg scan, exit ps at end *//* do one complete pass *//* avoid DFS channels, AP only *//* scan end, do DFS action *//* quantenna background scanning required *//* quantenna scanning on operating channel only *//* seach MBS, no action on scan end *//* OBSS scan *//* Note: top 4 bits for internal use only *//* got candidate, can stop *//* Prefer selecting DFS only channels for bootup CAC*//* Select channel from DFS and non-DFS sets which are available only*//* All Non-DFS channels are available by default,
 * DFS channels are available only after CAC-Completion events
 *//* pick a channel via a algorithm in a special domain *//*
   * Be aware only the lower 12 bits actually make it to ss_flags from
   * the flags parameter to ieee80211_start_scan.
   *//* # ssid's to probe/match *//* ssid's to probe/match *//* ordered channel set *//* ix of next chan to scan *//* ix + 1 of last chan to scan *//* min dwell on channel *//* min dwell time on a passive channel *//* max dwell on channel *//* max dwell time on a passive channel *//* used for calling ieee80211_start_scan() *//* was the channel scan initiated by supplicant *//*
 * The upper 16 bits of the flags word is used to communicate
 * information to the scanning code that is NOT recorded in
 * ss_flags.  It might be better to split this stuff out into
 * a separate variable to avoid confusion.
 *//* flush candidate table *//* don't update ssid list *//* Must use a result from the cache *//* Must keep the same wireless mode (11a, 11g, or 11at, etc) *//*
 * Parameters for managing cache entries:
 *
 * o a station with STA_FAILS_MAX failures is not considered
 *   when picking a candidate
 * o a station that hasn't had an update in STA_PURGE_SCANS
 *   (background) scans is discarded
 * o after STA_FAILS_AGE seconds we clear the failure count
 *//* assoc failures before ignored *//* time before clearing fails (secs) *//* age for purging sta entries (scans) *//* age for purging ap entries (scans) *//* pow2 to optimize out * and / *//* simple hash is enough for variation of macaddr *//* no response to mgmt frame *//* negative response to " " *//*
 * Parameters supplied when adding/updating an entry in a
 * scan cache.  Pointer variables should be set to NULL
 * if no data is available.  Pointer references can be to
 * local data; any information that is saved will be copied.
 * All multi-byte values must be in host byte order.
 *//* 802.11 capabilities *//* FHSS dwell interval *//* *//*
 * Scan cache entry format used when exporting data from a policy
 * module; this data may be represented some other way internally.
 *//* recv timestamp *//* from last rcv'd beacon *//* beacon interval (host byte order) *//* capabilities (host byte order) *//* channel where sta found *//* byte offset to TIM ie *//* FH only (host byte order) *//* FH only *//* ERP from beacon/probe resp *//* avg'd recv ssi *//* DTIM period *//* captured WPA ie *//* captured RSN ie *//* captured WME ie *//* captured WSC ie *//* captured HT Capability Info ie *//* captured HT Information ie *//* captured VHT Capability Info ie *//* captured VHT Operation Info ie *//* captured Atheros ie *//* captured qtn ie *//* captured Quantenna flags *//* 1 - is QTN device, 0 - non-QTN device *//* 0 - default mode, 1 - MBS, 2 - RBS *//* captured extender bssid ie *//* age of entry (0 on create) *//* local max transmit power from Beacon/Probe response *//*
 * Template for an in-kernel scan policy module.
 * Modules register with the scanning code and are
 * typically loaded as needed.
 *//* printable name *//* add an entry to the cache *//* age and/or purge entries in the cache *//* note that association failed for an entry *//* note that association succeed for an entry *//* iterate over entries in the scan cache *//* default action to take when found scan match *//* failure to associate count *//* seen during current scan *//* not seen in previous scans *//* LPF rssi state *//* time of last update *//* time of last failure *//* time of last association *//* iterator scan gen# *//* indicate that entry is in use and cannot be freed *//* indicate that entry must be freed after se_inuse cleared up *//* on scan table *//* all entries *//* on st_scangen *//* gen# for iterator *//* tasklet for "action" *//* selected bss for action tasklet *//* time of last update *//* LPF rssi state *//* seen during current scan *//* not seen in previous scans *//* indicate that entry is in use and cannot be freed *//* request to free entry after se_inuse cleared. *//* CCI, Co-Channel Interference *//* ACI, Adjacent Channel Interference *//* tasklet for "action" *//* selected bss for action tasklet *//* scan entry number *//* to protect as_scan_list *//* whether once used as working channel *//* CCA interference *//* tx and rx time *//* rssi from all STAs, used to calculate attenuation *//* 0.1db *//* the attenuation expected in low power channel *//* Recovered OEM461 scanner state and callbacks; no raw OEM IC offsets. *//* _NET80211_IEEE80211_SCAN_H_ *//*-
