 **//* Success definition in FWT Interface is return positive value *//* Error definition in FWT Interface is return negative value *//* specific commands keywords - must match fwt_if_usr_cmd *//* additional keywords *//* synchronise use of fwt_if_outbuf *//* set command keywords *//* value of extracted keywords from user *//* skip leading space *//* skip this word *//* replace spaces with NULL *//* clear node array *//*
		 * This keyword takes a MAC address or an IPv4 or IPv6 address. If it is a multicast
		 * IP address it is also converted into a multicast layer 2 (MAC) address.
		 *//* Port array names order correspond to HW port numbers *//*
 * Get the current value that attached to keyword definition
 * @param str: the string to find keyword
 * @param words: the target search
 * @param word_count: number of words to search from
 * @return: the value as a string
 *//* return the value attached to the keyword *//* advance to next word *//* ADD example: "add ab:34:be:af:34:42 port lhost node 2:4:3" *//* ADD_STATIC_MC example: "add_static_mc 224.51.2.3 mac ab:34:be:af:34:42*//* DEL_STATIC_MC example: "del_static_mc 224.51.2.3 mac ab:34:be:af:34:42*//* Must be called with the fwt_if_outbuf_lock held *//* a command was issued previously but the output was not retrieved *//* Apply user command.
 * User command can control the FWT interface.
 * @param cmd_num: command number
