 *//*
 * Quantenna HBM skb payload pool
 *//*
 * The vendor driver assumes HBM lives for the lifetime of the system.  The
 * OpenMitraStar RAM ladder intentionally unloads and warm-reloads it, so make
 * that lifecycle an explicit, target-owned operation rather than silently
 * applying it to other Topaz boards.
 *//*
 * The OEM timer called the blocking HBM request path with local IRQs masked.
 * On the Linux 5.10 RAM port that can starve the 1 Hz hardware-watchdog pet if
 * the completion pool state is stale.  TQE TX already reclaims synchronously
 * before consuming another payload, so keep timer reclaim opt-in while the
 * port is validated.  This parameter exists only in the v89/MitraStar build.
 *//*
 * Linux 5.10's ARC700 dma_cache_wback_inv() performs one cache-line
 * operation for the entire requested range while local IRQs are disabled.
 * The vendor HBM geometry contains 32 MiB and 34 MiB payload ranges, so a
 * single legacy flush can hide the exact failing operation and starve the
 * management/watchdog timers for an unnecessarily long interval.
 *
 * Keep the OEM memory geometry and final contents unchanged, but split the
 * poison+cache operation into bounded pieces on the explicitly gated HGW A2
 * port.  The range check is deliberately against the vendor/Linux boundary:
 * every HBM byte must remain below the first byte owned by Linux.
 *//* lower addr first *//* newest freed first *//* bad magic first *//* meaning dependent on sort type *//* meaning dependent on sort type *//* max dump number *//* bytes dump at head *//* bytes dump at tail *//* currently dumpped number *//* offsets for initial pool loading *//* Legacy proc diagnostics are not part of the packet data path. *//* always setup magic and guard area to provide minimum detection *//* only fix magic corruption when we are sure no one else is using it right now *//* shouldn't put it back to pool *//*
				 * Double free check is already broken because a lot of free places
				 * doesn't update the owner, both VB and PCIe platform.
				 *//*
				uint32_t *sizep = _m - HBM_HR_OFFSET_SIZE;
				const uint32_t size = arc_read_uncached_32(sizep);
				printk(KERN_ERR "%s: double free of buf_bus %p size %u owner %08x\n",
						__FUNCTION__, buf_bus, size, owner);
				topaz_hbm_buf_show(_p, TOPAZ_HBM_BUF_DUMP_DFT, 0);
				*//*
 * Safely return the buf.
 * @pkt_bus needn't to be the pointer from the pool. It can be any location in the buffer.
 *//*
	 * Do not infer "full" solely from equal masked pointers.  The raw HBM
	 * pointers are 16-bit monotonic counters; a corrupted or stale delta larger
	 * than the physical pool must never enter the unbounded request primitive.
	 *//* 12000 is over maximum vht frame size,
					and there is no rx frame whose size is over 12000 *//*
	 * Linux 5.10 has no pluggable skb allocator. Copy out of HBM and release
	 * the hardware buffer immediately; this preserves ownership safely.
	 *//* Linux networking requires the Ethernet header at +2 mod 4 so that the
	 * IPv4/IPv6 header following ETH_HLEN=14 is naturally 32-bit aligned.
	 * The OEM custom skb allocator provided this implicitly; the 5.10 copy
	 * path must reserve NET_IP_ALIGN explicitly for ARC700. *//* invalidate all packet dcache before passing to the kernel *//*
 * Allocate a new buffer to hold the pkt. The new buffer is guranteed to be safe from wmac rx dma overrun.
 * The original buffer is not used anymore. Caller should be responsible for freeing the buffer.
 *//* don't copy to new skb if it is aleady corrupted *//* copy from buffer head in case mac header is needed *//* caller only invalidate this pkt, not entire buffer *//* if corruption happens during data copying *//* reserve head space so that later caller's skb_put() covers the packet *//*
	 * Quarantine is done. now we are sure the data copy in skb is not corrupted and won't
	 *//* bubble sort *//* skip leading space *//* skip this word *//* replace spaces with NULL *//* Apply user command.
 * User command can control the HBM interface.
 * @param cmd_num: command number
 * @param words: the split words without spaces from the user space console interface
 * @param word_count: number of words after split
 * @return: status indication
 *//* Set null at last byte, note that count already gives +1 byte count*//* Extract command from first word *//* Exclude softirqs whilst manipulating forwarding table *//*
	 * OEM skb payload_free drained EMAC_TX_DONE on every skb release.  Linux
	 * 5.10 copies HBM payloads into normal skbs, so that allocator callback no
	 * longer exists.  Keep the hardware completion pool flowing independently
	 * of RX traffic.
	 *//* Fail closed before poisoning fixed HBM memory or rewriting pool CSRs. *//* Private provider-owned token, never a netdev/XMIT return code. *//**
 * Copyright (c) 2011-2012 Quantenna Communications, Inc.
 * All rights reserved.
 *
 * This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or
