 **//* SOURCE-ONLY provider owns bank state and all retained descriptions.
 * No recovery/release/reset API: first ownership pins both modules until reboot.
 * Entry count is bounded; saturated retention never overwrites previous records.
 * A missing slot is counted explicitly, not reported as complete ownership proof.
 *//* Typed batch reserves one PAYLOAD owner, not one descriptor per output.
 * Source fanout is bounded to128WMAC nodes plus7otherports; expectedrefs stay
 * attached to this one owner across partial submission or queue retention.
 *//* Acquire lifetime references BEFORE any skb/HBM mutation or TXSTART.
		 * Never rely on returning early from module_exit to prevent unloading. *//* known prepublication refusal can have no consumed payload *//* Fixed typed markers: one multicastbatch<=135 pendingoutputs.
 * Original queue ring owns each payloadref; markers persist token, neverstack.
 *//* A stored function pointer is already a lifetime dependency. Pin both
		 * modules before registration can outlive a failed batch admission. *//* Convert a pre-reserved global credit before the ordinary enqueue. *//* Pin before caller changes the payload's ec/freecount ownership. *//* A fixed slot is reserved now; timeout will never need new capacity. *//* Never recycle owned refs after refusal. *//* queued tokens remain valid untillastretry succeeds *//* Successful batch transfers all expected refs; recycle only its unused
		 * catalog slot. On quarantine retain the one owner with ALLexpectedrefs. *//* Missing callback/unfinished bank must remain a held owner and
			 * refuse all later writers, even when no poll timeout was observed. *//* Initial status setting *//* no HBM release while a bank output is uncertain *//* no unboundedHBMcleanup of typedowner *//* precedinguntypedhead mayhaveadvancedonto typedowner *//* retain queue and stop retry scheduling *//* defer nestedqueueconsumer beforetouching samehead *//* PNPT queue very likely is gone *//* keep head: NEVER retry, dequeue or free uncertain ownership *//* Typed owner/credit/head state is committed atomically. *//* retain container/tasklet context; modules pinned to reboot *//* The OEM path used DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL here. *//* The OEM crash-dump dispatcher is not part of mainline Linux 5.10. *//* Reconstructed from the live Topaz DBDC module and OEM MMU contract. *//* Compatibility include for pre-Kconfig-header Quantenna sources. *//*
 * Quantenna's 2.6.35 bridge hooks were private kernel extensions.  Linux
 * 5.10 has no public equivalent; declarations are added here as each caller
 * is moved to a supported bridge/FDB API.  Keep this header intentionally
 * inert so an accidental legacy hook cannot be linked into a test module.
 *//* Quantenna's private power-save QoS class removed from modern kernels. *//* Removed legacy APIs, preserving strlcpy return length rather than strscpy's
 * negative truncation result. Inputs obey the existing C-string contract. *//* The OEM linker placed selected hot paths in SRAM. Stage 1 keeps them in text. *//* Stage 1 uses the normal Linux bridge path, not Quantenna's private hooks. *//* IPv6 stays enabled in Linux; only qdrv's private NDISC hooks are omitted. *//* ARC ioremap() already creates the device mapping expected by this driver. *//* Entropy sampling was removed from request_irq(); no interrupt semantics. *//* Linux7.3removed in_irq alias: same hardIRQcount contract, not softIRQ. *//* Preserve original strncpy copy/pad/truncation semantics for historical ABI
 * buffers; replacing all callers with strscpy would alter nonterminated fields. *//* Exact Linux7.3 renamed timer API compatibility; no timing policy changes. *//* OEM register constants are CPU I/O addresses. Preserve MMIO ordering while
 * explicitly expressing pointer typing to modern Linux ARC accessors. *//* Preserve optionalexternalI2Csensorunavailability when kernelbusisabsent.
 * These guards do not emulate a sensor or report thermal acceptance. *//*
 * Linux 5.10 changed struct br_ip from one multicast address (`u`) to
 * source/destination fields.  qdrv's firmware ABI still carries the old
 * layout, so keep it under the legacy name while isolating the kernel type.
 *//* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 *//* OEM-only packet timing tracepoints; they do not affect datapath state. *//* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only *//* Caller serializes transitions. A retained reference has no release path:
 * F353 did not establish a safe hardware retirement contract. *//* Recovered v37.4.0.89 wire contract. Keep it versioned and unpublished. *//*
 * Recovered from qdrv_wlan_get_nac_info() in the OEM .89 qdrv module.
 * Keep the timestamp split into wire words: this makes the 4-byte ARC ABI
 * alignment explicit and avoids importing host compiler u64 alignment.
 *//*
 * MuC reads/writes the first three halfwords.  Their wider policy semantics
 * and the final 28 bytes are intentionally left opaque until matching .89
 * headers are recovered.  The allocation and entry array are exact.
 *//*
 * Exact .89 algorithm-control suffix of qtn_txbf_mbox.  Existing .62.1
 * controls move by four bytes; the final twelve bytes are firmware-owned and
 * remain opaque.  This is a substructure contract, not the complete mailbox.
 *//* Exact bounded .89 sublayout; the word at mailbox+0x1074 has no recovered name. *//*
 * .89 preserves the 32-entry circular ring and appends one cache-line-sized
 * special message slot selected by mailbox index 0xff.  It is not ring[33].
 *//*
 * Complete .89 TXBF wire image. The two byte-compatible regions retain the
 * proven .62.1 layout; only the inserted and appended opaque ranges differ.
 *//* W3_PAIR_APPROVED is zero: no caller may publish this wire object yet. *//**
