 **//* Search for an empty IOCTL *//* This is a purely blocking IOCTL. No real ring. *//* IOCTLs can be sent from non-sleep context. So we are forced to busy
	 * wait. MuC treats IOCTL msgs as highest prio task
	 *//* Serialize the empty check, publication and MuC doorbell. *//*
	 * Push msg into mbx
	 * - the current msg is offset into the dma region by ioctl index
	 *//* Order every descriptor/payload write before publishing command 6. *//* Interrupt MuC before another publisher can observe/reuse the mailbox. */// when in calibration mode, it takes long time. So, increase time-out period/* If too many failed IOCTLs, perform some system action (eg, panic, gather logs, whatever). *//* #ifdef MTEST *//*
		 * Linux 5.10 returns the ARC cached alias (0x8...) as the DMA
		 * handle.  The OEM helper expected a low bus address and maps an
		 * out-of-aperture value to zero.  Publishing that zero makes the
		 * mailbox look dequeued although MuC never receives the IOCTL.
		 *//* THese are the Per vap IOCLTS that finally go over the DEV ioctl *//*sys_rev_num*//* QTN_BG_SCAN *//* Allocate the Hostlink circular buffer *//* Make sure work queues are done *//* OEM482 source recovery: CALCMD first, then normalSETPARAM482. Payload6,
 * allocation128 and lowbyte powerencoding faithful. Source-only adaptation
 * retains unknown publishedDMA/descriptor and forbids retry/ownerteardown. *//* MACdead has legacyrawrc1 but publication=false; never call it ACK. *//* Required caller serialized RTNL/IC lifetime. Modulepin doesnotpinqw:
     * caller quiesce must refuse releasingIC/QDRV while pending query istrue. *//* Originalnormal command follows even calcmdalloc/error/refusal. *//* Permanently retain callerstate/radio/module/DMA until explicitrecovery.
     * No resets/frees/retry, and no followingnormal482 afterunknownCALCMD. */// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0/* Kernel-file API used by MuC requests and read-only board telemetry. *//**
