 **//*
 * The OEM RX path accidentally serializes the RX descriptor mailbox with
 * scan_if.scan_sem_bit even though qdrv_rx_init() imports the dedicated
 * host_rxfifo.rf_sem into rx_if.rx_sem_bit.  Apart from racing the MuC on the
 * RX FIFO, an unrelated scan owner can therefore strand NAPI forever in the
 * old unbounded while (!sem_take()) loop.  On a single-core ARC target that
 * presents exactly as a machine-wide hard lock: hard IRQs can still echo a
 * UART character, but no task or softirq makes forward progress.
 *
 * Keep the OEM semaphore choice everywhere else.  The corrected semaphore
 * and bounded acquisition are exclusive to the HGW-500BNA-QCv2 v89 port.
 *//* skb->data should be cache aligned - do calculation here to be sure. *//* buffer is set by MuC or AuC form hbm pool *//* FIXME Figure out which VAP device has the traffic *//* Use the first VAP for now *//*
	 * Rate limit checks - ensure we don't blindly process all of the
	 * possibly malicious data frames
	 *//*
 * Determines whether a frame should be accepted, based on information
 * about the frame's origin and encryption, and policy for this vap.
 *//*
	 * Data frames from unknown nodes should not make it here, but just in case...
	 *//* encrypted eapol is always OK *//* cleartext eapol is OK if we don't have pairwise keys yet *//* cleartext eapol is OK if configured to allow it *//* cleartext eapol is OK if other unencrypted is OK *//* not OK *//*
		 * Deny non-PAE frames received prior to authorization.  For
		 * open/shared-key authentication the port is mark authorized after
		 * authentication completes.  For 802.1X the port is not marked
		 * authorized by the authenticator until the handshake has completed.
		 *//*
		 * Frame received from external L2 filter will not have
		 * MAC header. So protection bit will be zero.
		 *//* Deny non-PAE frames received without encryption *//*
	 * AP will send mc/bc in 4 addr format packets, so drop this one if
	 * it is to be sent reliably.
	 *//*
* This function returns:
* 0 if DA remains untouched
* 1 if DA is changed by the qdrv bridge
*//*
	 * In case the current AP we are trying to associate didn't clean up for last session,
	 * don't wait for wpa_supplicant's next trying command which is 10s later.
	 * Give AP and STA some time to clean up and then try again quickly.
	 *//*
 * qtn_rx_decap() reuses space inside the 802.11 frame for the Ethernet
 * header.  The resulting offset depends on the 802.11 header length, so an
 * HBM skb that starts aligned can still reach Linux with its IPv4/IPv6
 * header at +2 mod 4.  ARC700 traps on the 32-bit loads used by the 5.10 IP
 * stack.  The OEM kernel tolerated this through its private skb/unaligned
 * machinery; the upstream 5.10 boundary must provide NET_IP_ALIGN itself.
 *
 * Keep HBM ownership unchanged: skb_copy_expand() makes a normal Linux skb,
 * copies the complete header metadata, and the caller frees the old HBM-copy
 * skb only after the replacement exists.  The runtime gate is populated once
 * in qdrv_rx_init(), and this code is not compiled outside the pinned v89
 * pair.
 *//*
	 * In Amber WOWLAN is handled by WIFI2SOC interrupt.
	 *//* qdrv_rx_vlan_ingress() still consumes di->start from the original
	 * decap buffer.  Realign only after that final user, before
	 * handle_rx_msdu() calls eth_type_trans(). *//*
 * check the data frame is valid or not.
 *//*
 * Decap the incoming frame.
 * Returns 0 if the frame has been consumed, else 1.
 *//* Include probe requests in the bounded trace.  A visible beacon with
		 * no probe/auth frames distinguishes a client selecting another BSSID
		 * from a hostapd authentication failure, without logging client MACs. *//* QTN_BG_SCAN *//*
			 * FIXME
			 * skb->src_port may be wrong.
			 * For WLAN_OVER_WDS_P2P test, AP may think that Beacon frames sent by its
			 * WDS peers to be from associated STAs by mistake.
			 * Dig into this issue deeply later.
			 *//* Pass up some data packets from unknown stations, so a deauth can be sent *//* Silently drop frames from blacklisted stations *//*
		 * Store the RSSI value previously calculated.
		 *//* if the node is unauthorized, a deauth should be sent by the sta*//*
			 * The HGW AuC data path bypasses ieee80211_input(), while the
			 * legacy inactivity timer only observes MuC shared counters.  A
			 * valid uplink data frame from an associated station is direct
			 * proof of liveness, so mirror the normal net80211 RX refresh here.
			 *//* Pass up non-data, fragmented data for reassembly, or data from unknown nodes *//* Rate limit these *//* check tdls *//*
	 * Set pointers in pointer array to the descriptors in the
	 * descriptor array
	 *//* Linux 5.10 keeps bridge snooping state private; bridge owns filtering. *//* drop if Intra BSS isolation enabled *//* If enabled, always send back LNCB and SSDP packets to the BSS *//*
	 * Deliver the IGMP frames to linux bridge module
	 * Send non-snooped multicast back to the BSS
	 *//* hit from bridge table, drop it since it is probably a multicast echo *//* hit from bridge table, drop it since it is probably a multicast echo *///CONFIG_BRIDGE.../*
 * 1. Save IP corresponding MAC Address to database
 * 2. Replace MAC for corresponding IP in packets
 * 3. Replace MAC for existing IP in database
 *
 * Fixme: when should we remove these nodes?
 *//* First IP to store in database *//* Replace current packets *//* IP Already here but MAC may be changed *//* Save corresponding IP and MAC to database as a new entry *//*
 * Replace Source MAC Address and BOOTP Client Address with Client Identifier
 *//* Recalculate the UDP checksum *//* Add psuedo IP header checksum *//* 0 is converted to -1 *//*
		 * Set the destination MAC address
		 * - if in 4-address mode or the frame is multicast, use the supplied DA
		 * - if 3-address bridge mode is enabled, get the DA from the qdrv bridge
		 * - in standard 3-address mode, use the bridge device's MAC
		 *   address as the destination (if found), otherwise use the supplied DA
		 *//* Check if node is authorized to receive *//* FIXME If EAPOL need passing externally, this needs fixing up *//*
	 * If the destination is multicast, LNCB, or another node on the BSS, send the packet back
	 * to the BSS.
	 *//* defined(CONFIG_BRIDGE) || defined(CONFIG_BRIDGE_MODULE) *//* no matter if new buf is used, no need for original one *//* Init pending list of skb to be indicated *//* Process left over from last poll *//* No previous data. *//* Nothing more to process *//* Check descriptor *//* This skb has been given to DSP for action frame *//*
			DBGPRINTF_E("No buffer for descriptor 0x%08x\n",
					(unsigned int) rxdesc);
			*//* Prepare the skb *//*
		 * CCMP MIC error frames may be decapsulated into garbage packets
		 * with invalid MAC DA, messing up the forwarding table.
		 *//* Decap the 802.11 frame into one or more (A-MSDU) Ethernet frames *//*
			 * Let's break loop, current descriptor will be added to pending.
			 * Next time we will try to allocate again.
			 *//*
		 * Get the physical ring pointer we are going to process now
		 * and pass the previous pointer to the MuC. There is 1 descriptor
		 * as buffer zone to prevent overwrites.
		 *//*
		 * Get next descriptor.
		 *//* Tell MuC that descriptor is returned *//* MBSS - Napi is scheduled for vnet[0] so napi_complete should map to correct VAP *//* qv1 = qv at start of this function stores correct VAP for this purpose *//*
 * we can't get how many layers MUC has applied on this packet
 * through tqe interface.
 * but current vlan code indicate only one layer, so just remove it.
 * *//*
 * Frame received from external L2 filter will not have MAC header
 * So whole_frm_hdr will be NULL for those frames.
 *//* skb_copy_expand() may change headroom and only preserves the tail of
		 * the old headroom.  whole_frm_hdr commonly points at the beginning of
		 * that headroom on the quarantine path, so rebasing an old skb->head
		 * offset into the replacement skb is not valid.  Copy the short-lived
		 * 802.11 header before qdrv_rx_stack_align() can free the old skb. *//* Never retain a pointer into an skb that alignment may replace. *//* The direct TQE path bypasses qdrv_rx_decap_callback(), so it must
		 * establish the same ARC-safe Ethernet-to-L3 alignment before
		 * handle_rx_msdu() calls eth_type_trans().  VLAN translation changes
		 * the frame length by four bytes and therefore preserves mod-4. *//**
