**//* Preserve the OEM v89 host fields; rewrite only MuC wire aliases. *//* This fucntion allocates a beacon ie and associate the beacon ie buffer. *//* convert to bus address for MuC access only *//* to avoid memory remap, keep lhost original buffer address for debug purpose *//* Preserved original algorithm for source provenance. *//*
 * This function allocates an ie descriptor, construct it with ie payload buffer and
 * queue it to the list
 *//* This function is same as above but always append the descriptor as header. *//* if header wasn't there, then we need setup tail as same as header *//* Reserved dynamic slots are allocated once per unpublished beacon build.
 * Repeated CCA/APP updates never advance curr or enlarge the MuC wire arena. *//* Inspect the entire unpublished chain before rewiring any prefix. *//* Wire traversal must match frame order, including APP-first/CCA-later. *//* This query is used by QDRV before its hostlink publication. *//* Frame extents are checked at complete-state boundaries, before payload writes
 * and again before QDRV publication. Temporary relocation gaps are unpublished. *//* Flush the liner memory so that MuC can rebuild the beacon ie via link list *//* This free the descriptor memory and reset the parameters *//* Check the exact next slot before touching payload bytes. *//*
	 * Always queue the beacon frame header on the list header position so that MuC
	 * can compose the frame easily.
	 *//* Check the exact next slot before touching payload bytes. *//*
 * This function provides a common interface to add ie field, ext_ie_id is extended to
 * support same IE id in different descriptors.
