 * This function works for both AP and STA.
 *//* Unit: Kbps *//* Unit: second, 32bits should be up to 136 years *//* Correct pseudo RSSIs that apparently still get into the node table *//* The node iterator may hold scan/node locks. Keep all user access outside. *//* Never dereference the userspace ioctl pointer directly. *//*
	 * qcsapi's association-count query requests the complete legacy station
	 * table through SIOCDEVPRIVATE+0xb. Linux holds RTNL around that ioctl and
	 * the legacy implementation then acquires the scan and node-table locks.
